","lemma":"ஏம்","gloss":"first person plural pronominal suffix"}],"gloss":"we women"},{"surface":"அல்லேம்","parts":[{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"not"},{"text":"ஏம்","lemma":"ஏம்","gloss":"first person plural suffix"}],"gloss":"we are not"},{"surface":"மாதோ","parts":[{"text":"மாதோ","lemma":"மாதோ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருங்காட்டுப்","parts":[{"text":"பெருங்காட்டுப்","lemma":"பெருங்காட்டுப்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பண்ணிய","parts":[{"text":"பண்ணிய","lemma":"பண்ணிய","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கருங்கோட்டு","parts":[{"text":"கருங்கோட்டு","lemma":"கருங்கோட்டு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஈமம்","parts":[{"text":"ஈமம்","lemma":"ஈமம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"நுமக்கு","parts":[{"text":"நுமக்கு","lemma":"நுமக்கு","gloss":"to you"}],"gloss":"to you","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அரிது","parts":[{"text":"அரிது","lemma":"அரிது","gloss":"difficult"}],"gloss":"difficult"},{"surface":"ஆகுக","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"become"},{"text":"க","lemma":"க","gloss":"optative suffix"}],"gloss":"let it be"},{"surface":"தில்ல","parts":[{"text":"தில்ல","lemma":"தில்ல","gloss":"particle of desire"}],"gloss":"indeed/may it"},{"surface":"எமக்கு","parts":[{"text":"எமக்கு","lemma":"எமக்கு","gloss":"to us"}],"gloss":"to us","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"எம்","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"யாம்","gloss":"our"}],"gloss":"our"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருந்தோள்","parts":[{"text":"பெருமை","lemma":"பெருமை","gloss":"greatness/broadness"},{"text":"தோள்","lemma":"தோள்","gloss":"shoulder"}],"gloss":"broad shoulders"},{"surface":"கணவன்","parts":[{"text":"கணவன்","lemma":"கணவன்","gloss":"husband"}],"gloss":"husband"},{"surface":"மாய்ந்து","parts":[{"text":"மாய்ந்து","lemma":"மாய்ந்து","gloss":"having died"}],"gloss":"having died","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"since/as"}],"gloss":"since"},{"surface":"அரும்பு","parts":[{"text":"அரும்பு","lemma":"அரும்பு","gloss":"bud"}],"gloss":"bud"},{"surface":"அற","parts":[{"text":"அறு","lemma":"அறு","gloss":"cease/cut off"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"completely"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வள்","parts":[{"text":"வள்","lemma":"வள்","gloss":"strong/abundant"}],"gloss":"abundant"},{"surface":"இதழ்","parts":[{"text":"இதழ்","lemma":"இதழ்","gloss":"petal"}],"gloss":"petal"},{"surface":"அவிழ்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"அவிழ்ந்த","lemma":"அவிழ்ந்த","gloss":"blossomed"}],"gloss":"blossomed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தாமரை","parts":[{"text":"தாமரை","lemma":"தாமரை","gloss":"lotus"}],"gloss":"lotus"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நள்","parts":[{"text":"நள்","lemma":"நள்","gloss":"deep/middle"}],"gloss":"deep"},{"surface":"இரும்","parts":[{"text":"இரும்","lemma":"இரும்","gloss":"dark/great"}],"gloss":"dark"},{"surface":"பொய்கையும்","parts":[{"text":"பொய்கை","lemma":"பொய்கை","gloss":"pond"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and (conjunctive)"}],"gloss":"and the pond"},{"surface":"தீயும்","parts":[{"text":"தீ","lemma":"தீ","gloss":"fire"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and (conjunctive)"}],"gloss":"and the fire"},{"surface":"ஓரற்றே","parts":[{"text":"ஓரற்றே","lemma":"ஓரற்றே","gloss":"are of the same nature"}],"gloss":"are of the same nature","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"O many wise ones! O many wise ones! / Who prevent me saying 'stay back' without saying 'go', / O many wise ones of evil counsel! / Sliced with a knife, cooked curved cucumber, / without touching fragrant ghee, fine and white like seed, / squeezed by hand, the ball of rice lying among leaves, / cooked with white sesame paste and sour tamarind, / with boiled vēḷai greens as food, / dwelling without a mat on a bed strewn with pebbles, / we are not grieving women indeed! / The funeral pyre of black logs prepared in the great cremation ground, / let it be difficult for you, may it be! To us, our / broad-shouldered husband having died, completely / blossomed lotus with abundant petals, / the deep, dark pond and the fire are of the same nature!","translation":"O wise men! O wise men! You who do not say 'go' but hold me back, saying 'stay', O wise men of cruel counsel! I am not one of those miserable widows who eat only hand-squeezed balls of rice served on leaves, cooked with sour tamarind and white sesame paste, without even a drop of fragrant ghee that looks like white seeds, along with boiled vēḷai greens, and who sleep on a bed of pebbles without a mat. To you, the funeral pyre of black logs built in the vast cremation ground may seem terrifying. But to me, since my broad-shouldered husband is dead, the fire is no different from a deep, cool pond where lotus buds have fully blossomed.","modern":"பல அறிவுடைய சான்றோர்களே! பல அறிவுடைய சான்றோர்களே! என்னை 'உடன் செல்க' என்று சொல்லாமல், 'இங்கே தங்கிவிடு' என்று தடுத்து நிறுத்தும் தீய அறிவுரை கூறும் சான்றோர்களே! வெள்ளரிப் பிஞ்சை வாளால் அரிந்து சமைத்து, விதையைப் போன்ற வெள்ளையான நறுமண நெய்யைத் தொடாமல், இலைகளுக்கு இடையே வைத்து கைகளால் பிழிந்த சோற்றுத் திரளையை, வெள்ளை எள் விழுதும் புளியும் சேர்த்துச் சமைத்த வேளைக் கீரையோடு உணவாக உண்டு, பருக்கைக் கற்கள் பரப்பிய படுக்கையில் பாய் இல்லாமல் படுத்துக் கிடந்து வருந்தும் கைம்பெண் அல்லேன் நான்! சுடுகாட்டில் கரிய விறகுகளால் அமைக்கப்பட்ட இந்த ஈமத்தீ உங்களுக்குக் கொடியதாகத் தோன்றலாம். ஆனால், என் தோள்வலிமை மிக்க கணவன் மறைந்த பிறகு, இதழ்கள் விரிந்த தாமரைகள் நிறைந்த குளிர்ந்த பொய்கையும், இந்த எரியும் தீயும் எனக்கு ஒன்றுதான்!","explanation":"This poem is spoken by Perunkōppeṇṭu, the queen of King Pūtapāṇṭiyaṉ, as she prepares to perform sati (self-immolation) on her husband's funeral pyre. The court elders and wise men try to dissuade her, advising her to live as a widow. She rejects their counsel, describing the harsh, ascetic life of a widow—eating tasteless, hand-squeezed rice with boiled greens and sleeping on pebbles—and declares she is not such a weak woman. She asserts that while the funeral pyre of black logs may seem terrifying to them, to her, now that her beloved husband is gone, the burning fire is as cool and welcoming as a deep pond filled with blooming lotuses. The poem belongs to the Potuviyal tiṇai and Āṉantap Paiyuḷ tuṟai, capturing the profound grief of a widow who chooses death over a life of forced asceticism.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}